+++ b/qualification/act1-action-cell-20261108/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# ACT-1: tool and action Cell execution semantics
+
+This package develops the sixth Hepta Cell role: versioned, composable action
+skills whose success is checked against destination-owned effects. The starting
+candidate is `6ddfca2406e4d01416cd2f7ab1655a0dc16f8da5`, tree
+`491eace326f335498334fb051c9e8f298ca7a04c`, on
+`fix/codex-v13-same-model-next-task-20261106`. It is distinct from the observed
+default branch `732e934ba496d90fbe042b8d41d479ef901643e5`.
+
+## Scope and authority
+
+The implementation extends the existing `automation.taskflow` authorized-effect
+path. It retains the producer-owned operation identity, exact immutable provider
+payload, FinalUse authority, durable dispatch-attempt ledger and reconciliation
+rules. It does not create another execution kernel or grant authority to a Cell
+proposal. The experimental destination is a controlled local service, not a
+production external account.
+
+The skill contract binds initiation, internal policy, termination, goal
+postcondition, version, bounded call resources and recovery. Registered, independently provisioned host observers actually evaluate initiation,
+termination and goal predicates. These are not automatically learned predicates;
+the policy digest pins an implementation identity rather than adding a policy interpreter. An envelope binds the skill contract and destination into the
+same bytes already covered by the provider payload digest and FinalUse grant.
+
+The goal-checked driver independently observes the destination after a provider
+completion claim and during recovery. Its durable receipt binds the original
+operation/key, payload, destination, skill contract and independent goal evidence.
+Transport completion, exit status and a cancellation request are separate from
+goal satisfaction. A partial effect never authorizes replay of the entire action.
+An unresolved operation keeps its original identity and is reconciled; neither
+silence nor a failed lookup proves absence. This change also fixes the existing
+`ProviderEffectTaskFlowDriver`: ordinary `NotFound` is now `Unresolved`, matching
+the provider contract journal, instead of granting `ProvenAbsent` retry rights.
+A fresh independent no-effect/no-late-commit proof is a stronger domain contract.
+
+Call bounds are not a claim of globally durable resource accounting. Cross-call
+and cross-restart expenditure belongs to the existing task/circuit owner. A
+future learned policy must consume that same persisted budget.
+
+## ACT-1 acceptance matrix
+
+| Injection | Independent destination fact | Required behavior |
+|---|---|---|
+| Effect committed, ACK lost | Effect row exists once | Keep identity, recover by lookup, no second mutation |
+| Waiting for input | Process is waiting and goal is absent | No false completion or duplicate process |
+| Partial success | Only a strict subset of required effects exists | Preserve partial evidence and remain unresolved |
+| Cancel before completion | No completed target effect | Cancellation delivery alone does not certify absence |
+| Completion before cancel | Target effect remains committed | Observed completion wins without erasing cancellation history |
+| Owner restart mid-operation | Durable attempt survives | Reconcile the original operation without redispatch |
+| Exit zero without target effect | Goal is absent despite successful exit | Reject the success claim |
+| Unobservable/unsupported destination | No trustworthy outcome can be recovered | Keep UNKNOWN, no blind retry |
+| Key, payload or contract drift | Observation belongs to different identity | Reject cross-binding evidence |
+
+The reliable baselines are deterministic persistent workflows, hand-authored DSL
+macros and flat skills. They must share the destination, oracle, fault schedule,
+observation capabilities and budget. A naive return-code policy may be a negative
+control, but beating it is not evidence of a Cell-specific learning benefit.
+
+## Evidence and interpretation
+
+Native gate records and exact counts are retained beside this file after the
+scoped run. They bind the executed source tree and the test log/JUnit run identity.
+Failed build/test attempts remain in the package. The cancellation injection is a destination cancellation request, not the
+TaskFlow run `Cancel` command. The SIGKILL test reopens the same owner fence;
+it is not a new-epoch/two-writer recovery proof. Input waiting uses an actual
+stdin reader and authoritative destination state; it is not RECEIPT syscall
+detection or a formal proof of input delivery order. The full product rollout,
+remote `runtime.codex` binding, real task distribution and learned hierarchy
+generalization require their own evidence; the local controlled ACT-1 run does
+not establish those claims.
+
+After the execution contract is fixed, compare learned hierarchy, proximal
+feedback prediction and residual-driven local adaptation. Freeze each policy's
+model, training/tuning opportunities and full budget. Hold out composition
+structures and task sources rather than merely changing identifiers. Count
+failure, cancellation and timeout episodes in the denominator. Report actual
+business success, false success, duplicate effects, unresolved outcomes, unsafe
+retry, recovery calls/time and all learning/inference costs.
+
+## Research basis, verified 2026-11-08
+
+* Perks et al., [Connectome analysis of a cerebellum-like circuit for sensory
+  prediction](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10690-6), Nature,
+  2026-09-02. Connectomics, recording and constrained models motivate a
+  proximal-prediction/residual-adaptation hypothesis. They do not establish
+  software transaction correctness or an advantage for this implementation.
+* Harvey et al., [Unsupervised Hierarchical Skill Discovery, v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2601.23156v2), 2026-05-28. Structure discovery uses
+  unlabeled observational trajectories; grounding downstream executable policies
+  still uses action labels and initiation/termination mechanisms.
+* Physical Intelligence et al., [pi0.5](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16054),
+  2025-04-22. High-level semantic and low-level robotic actions motivate a
+  hierarchy comparison, not a software-recovery guarantee.
+* Yang et al., [RECEIPT, v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2611.01930v1), 2026-11-01.
+  Distinguishes return, input wait and actual task effect, and checks a bounded
+  intervention protocol. Its finite-model assumptions do not prove universal
+  exactly-once external execution.
